# jiuyue monitor environment template.
#
# Installed by deploy/provision.sh to /etc/jiuyue/monitor.env (mode 0640,
# root:root) and loaded by jiuyue-monitor.service via EnvironmentFile=.
# Everything here is read by deploy/monitor/monitor.sh.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy: this is server state. This template carries
# placeholders only. The webhook URL is a credential (anyone who has it can post
# into your alert channel) and must not enter git.

# --- where alerts go --------------------------------------------------------
#
# A plain JSON webhook. The monitor POSTs one object per alert, e.g.
#   {"source":"jiuyue-monitor","host":"...","event":"disk_usage",
#    "severity":"critical","target":"/","value":92,"threshold":90,
#    "message":"...","text":"[critical] disk_usage /: ...","timestamp":"..."}
# `text` is a pre-rendered human line, so a generic relay, ntfy, Slack or a chat
# bot can consume it without a custom adapter.
#
# Leave the placeholder until a real endpoint exists. An empty value means a
# triggered alert is only logged (and the unit fails), so NOBODY is paged.
ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.com/REPLACE_WITH_WEBHOOK_TOKEN

# --- alert policy -----------------------------------------------------------
# Re-send a still-firing alert at most once per cooldown; a *new* severity or a
# cleared condition is sent immediately regardless.
ALERT_COOLDOWN_SEC=3600
# Send a one-shot `recovery` notice when a condition clears (1) or stay silent (0).
ALERT_NOTIFY_RECOVERY=1
# State, the restart record and status.json live here. Survives a reboot.
ALERT_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/jiuyue-monitor
# Override the host label in the payload (defaults to `hostname`).
# ALERT_HOSTNAME=

# --- what to check ----------------------------------------------------------
# Services asserted `systemctl is-active`. `postgresql` is the Debian meta unit
# (covers postgresql@16-main); add coturn/livekit here when they are deployed.
MONITOR_SERVICES=jiuyue caddy postgresql

# Filesystems whose use% is watched. Add /var when it is a separate mount.
DISK_PATHS=/
# Warning at >=80%, critical at >=90%. Alert early: waiting until 95% leaves no
# room to clean up (docs/research/2026-09-16-vps-2gb-ops-research.md §(g)).
DISK_WARN_PERCENT=80
DISK_CRIT_PERCENT=90

# MemAvailable as a percentage of MemTotal. Below ~10-15% is the documented
# "swap in/out is about to start" zone (research §(c)).
MEM_AVAILABLE_WARN_PERCENT=15
MEM_AVAILABLE_CRIT_PERCENT=8

# A service must fail this many consecutive one-minute checks before alerting,
# so a single in-flight restart (a deploy) does not page anyone.
SERVICE_DOWN_STRIKES=2

# --- crash-loop detection ---------------------------------------------------
# `Restart=always` on jiuyue.service hides crashes by design. This counts
# systemd's automatic restarts ("Scheduled restart job") in a sliding window: a
# single restart during a deploy is normal, RESTART_THRESHOLD in the window is a
# crash loop. Every observed change in NRestarts is appended to
# ${ALERT_STATE_DIR}/restarts.log with a reason.
RESTART_SERVICE=jiuyue
RESTART_WINDOW_SEC=600
RESTART_THRESHOLD=5
